## Context

Reading-3 (tracker [[0605]]). Two coupled things in §5 and across the body:
a specific paragraph replacement, and a sweep of experimental-history
bookkeeping into the annex.

## A. Replace the whole "Cohorts." paragraph

Current (`slides/manuscript/main.tex:496–500`):

> \textbf{Cohorts.} The sweep dispatched 16 models. Two were dropped
> before analysis, leaving the 14-model analysis cohort that backs every
> per-model number, Figure~… Every figure caption below names the cohort
> it draws on.

Replace the ENTIRE paragraph with one sentence (author's words):

> We present results for a cohort of \NumCensusModels{} models of
> assorted sizes, from five leading AI labs (see
> Figure~\ref{fig:capability-timeline}).

Notes:
- Use the macro `\NumCensusModels` (=14), not a typed "14".
- "see Figure 2" → `\ref{fig:capability-timeline}` (house rule: no
  hardcoded figure numbers).
- **FIVE labs** (author confirmed 2026-06-15, not four): consistent with
  Figure 2's "five leading AI labs" (`:469`). The Exp 1 cohort spans all
  five (Anthropic, OpenAI/GPT-OSS, DeepSeek, Mistral, Alibaba/Qwen) —
  verify the five-lab span against the cohort in
  `experiments/models.yaml` / the analysis cohort before finalizing.

## B. Sweep experimental-history bookkeeping into the annex

Author: "The experimental history considerations belong to the annex.
Talking about 16 runs in the main manuscript only confuses the reader.
Sweep."

- The "16 models dispatched / 2 dropped" detail (and any like it —
  dispatch counts, dropped/excluded models, run-history, sweep mechanics)
  moves OUT of the main body (§1–§9 + Conclusion) and INTO the relevant
  annex (Exp 1 spec `sec:annex-exp1` / Exp 2 spec `sec:annex-exp2`).
  Verify the detail is preserved in the annex (don't just delete it).
- SWEEP the whole body for this class: phrasings about how many models
  were dispatched/dropped, pilot/excluded runs, harness run-bookkeeping.
  The main text keeps the analysis cohort (\NumCensusModels) and the
  findings; the provenance of how the cohort was assembled lives in the
  annex (this aligns with the standalone-text policy, [[0606]]).

## C. Iron out the cohort-description redundancy (author-flagged)

The §5 "\textbf{Experiment 1 — Parametric baseline.}" paragraph
(`main.tex:519`) ALSO describes the cohort: "We query the fourteen … they
are listed on Figure~\ref{fig:reliability} and include Claude, DeepSeek,
Mistral and Qwen at various sizes from workstation to frontier" (set by
reading-2 finding 30). With the new one-sentence Cohorts summary (A), the
cohort is now described twice in §5.
- Reconcile so the cohort is introduced ONCE. Options: fold the new
  one-sentence summary into the Experiment-1 paragraph, or keep the
  summary and trim the duplicate clause from `:519`. Author/executor
  picks; the result must not state the cohort size/labs/sizes twice.
- Watch consistency: the summary references Figure 2 (labs), the `:519`
  sentence references Figure 5 (reliability list) — keep both figure
  pointers if both are wanted, but say the cohort facts once.

